The root cause: `deepEqual([], {})` reached the key-comparison stage with both having zero keys, and since neither matched the custom-prototype guard, it fell through to `return true`. I added an early check that returns `false` when exactly one of the two values is an array:

```ts
if (Array.isArray(object1) !== Array.isArray(object2)) {
  return false;
