```

This is symmetric, so it covers both `deepEqual([], {})` and `deepEqual({}, [])`. It also handles the nested cases (`{ items: [] }` vs `{ items: {} }`) because nested values recurse through `deepEqual`, and it doesn't affect array-vs-array or object-vs-object comparisons.
